        "date": "2026-11-27T16:06:45Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): the Klartext post writes cycles 200, 206, 207 and the cycle 9 dwell\n\nThe Heidenhain Klartext post writes the drilling cycles of the iTNC 530\nNC 340490-03 at the q211 parameter level: cycle 200 with Q202 = the\nwhole depth for DRILL and SPOT, cycle 207 for a rigid tap, cycle 206 for\na floating tap, and cycle 9 for the dwell of PECK and DEEP. PECK and\nDEEP keep the checked chain as L blocks (#4224). Each replaced chain\nmove is compared with the cycle's own motion; a chain that differs is\nrefused by name. A drill or a tap cuts only inside its drilling cycle.\n\nFixes #4227\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
